// Portappix application and tray icons.
//
// The source artwork lives in the repository folder "portappix_icons\":
// the .ico files there are PNG-compressed (fine for Windows, but the
// resource compiler cannot embed PNG icon entries and a PNG entry is not
// a valid RT_ICON resource). scripts\convert_icons.py therefore produces
// the DIB-compressed copies in "portappix_icons\dib\" that this script
// embeds:
//
//   python scripts/convert_icons.py
//   brcc32 src\PortappixIcons.rc -fo src\PortappixIcons.res
//
// Run brcc32 from the repository root: the paths below are resolved
// relative to the current directory.
//
// Resource ids (see src\Portappix.Icons.pas, which loads them):
//
//   1  ICON    portappix.ico              application / launcher icon
//   2  ICON    portappix-tray-normal.ico  tray: idle, apps installed
//   3  ICON    portappix-tray-running.ico tray: an app is running
//   4  ICON    portappix-tray-paused.ico  tray: an update is pending
//   5  ICON    portappix-tray-error.ico   tray: the last operation failed
//   6  ICON    portappix-tray-inactive.ico tray: no apps installed
//
//  10  RCDATA  portappix-app.png          application artwork for the UI

1  ICON    "portappix_icons\\dib\\portappix.ico"
2  ICON    "portappix_icons\\dib\\portappix-tray-normal.ico"
3  ICON    "portappix_icons\\dib\\portappix-tray-running.ico"
4  ICON    "portappix_icons\\dib\\portappix-tray-paused.ico"
5  ICON    "portappix_icons\\dib\\portappix-tray-error.ico"
6  ICON    "portappix_icons\\dib\\portappix-tray-inactive.ico"
10 RCDATA  "portappix_icons\\portappix-app.png"
